module
public import MMP.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.FrobeniusSplittingCocycles
import MMP.AlgebraicGeometry.Positivity.RelativeSemiampleGeneration
import MMP.AlgebraicGeometry.Positivity.SemiampleSectionModule
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FiniteType.LocallyNoetherian

/-!
# The logarithmic Cartier isomorphism, the Deligne–Illusie decomposition, and section modules

Let `k` be a perfect field of characteristic `p > 0`, let `B` be a smooth `k`-algebra and let
`t : ι → B` be a finite family of functions cutting out a reduced simple normal crossing divisor
`S = ∑ⱼ V(tⱼ)` on `V = Spec B`. The logarithmic forms `Ω^i_{B/k}(log S)` are the forms on the
complement `B[1/∏ⱼ tⱼ]` spanned over `B` by wedges of the one-forms `db` (`b ∈ B`) and
`dlog tⱼ = tⱼ⁻¹ dtⱼ`. They form a sub-differential-graded algebra of the de Rham complex of the
complement, and the de Rham differential is `B`-linear on `F_*Ω^•_{B/k}(log S)`, where `b`
acts as `bᵖ`.

The **inverse Cartier isomorphism** is the isomorphism of graded algebras
`C⁻¹ : Ω^i_{B/k}(log S) ⟶ H^i(F_*Ω^•_{B/k}(log S))`, Frobenius-semilinear (`b ω ↦ bᵖ C⁻¹ ω`),
with `C⁻¹(db) = [b^{p-1} db]` and `C⁻¹(dlog tⱼ) = [dlog tⱼ]`.

Let `k` be a perfect field of characteristic `p`, let `V` be a smooth proper `k`-scheme of
relative dimension `n < p`, and let `S = ∑ⱼ Sⱼ` be a simple normal crossing divisor on `V`.
Suppose the pair `(V, S)` lifts to a smooth scheme `𝒱` over `W₂(k)` together with a relative
simple normal crossing divisor `𝒮 = ∑ⱼ 𝒮ⱼ` restricting to `S`. Then the Frobenius pushforward
`F_*Ω^•_{V/k}(log S)` of the logarithmic de Rham complex decomposes in the derived category of
`𝒪`-modules as the direct sum of its cohomology sheaves `Ω^i(log S)[-i]`, `0 ≤ i ≤ n`.

Let `f : Y ⟶ S` be a projective morphism to a locally Noetherian scheme, `L` an invertible
`𝒪_Y`-module which is relatively semiample (every point of `S` has an open neighbourhood `U`
over which some positive tensor power `L^{⊗ d}` is generated by its sections over `f⁻¹(U)`), and
`F` a coherent `𝒪_Y`-module. Then the graded `𝒪_S`-module
`𝓜(F, L) = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} f_*(F ⊗ L^{⊗ n})` is locally finite over the graded `𝒪_S`-algebra
`𝓡(L) = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} f_* L^{⊗ n}`: over every affine open `U ⊆ S` the module of sections
`⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(f⁻¹(U), F ⊗ L^{⊗ n})` is finitely generated over `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(f⁻¹(U), L^{⊗ n})`.

## Main results

* `MMP.DeRham.exists_logInverseCartier`: the inverse Cartier isomorphism for the logarithmic
  de Rham complex of a simple normal crossing divisor on a smooth affine `k`-scheme.
* `MMP.DeRham.nonempty_logDeRham_decomposition_of_wittTwoLift`: the decomposition
  `⨁_{i ≤ n} Ω^i_{V/k}(log S)[-i] ≅ F_*Ω^•_{V/k}(log S)` for a pair lifting to `W₂(k)`.
* `MMP.moduleFinite_twistModule_restrict_of_isProjective`: the module of twisted sections of
  `F` restricted to `f⁻¹(U)` is a finite module over the section ring of `L` restricted to
  `f⁻¹(U)`, for every affine open `U ⊆ S`.

## Implementation notes

*The inverse Cartier isomorphism.* The source states the isomorphism for the sheaves
`Ω^i_{V^{(1)}/k}(log S^{(1)})` on the Frobenius twist `V^{(1)}`. Because `k` is perfect,
`V^{(1)} ≅ V` as schemes with the `k`-structure twisted by Frobenius, and
`Ω^i_{V^{(1)}/k}(log S^{(1)})` is `Ω^i_{V/k}(log S)` with `b` acting through `bᵖ`; a map out of
it is a Frobenius-semilinear map out of `Ω^i_{V/k}(log S)`. The sheaf statement is local and the
map is determined by its values on `db` and `dlog tⱼ`, which do not depend on the chart. So it is
equivalent to the statement on the affine opens where every component is principal, and that is
the form given here.

The simple normal crossing condition is that at every prime `𝔭` of `B` the differentials of
the `tⱼ` lying in `𝔭` are linearly independent in the fibre `κ(𝔭) ⊗_B Ω_{B/k}`. Over a perfect
field this is the same as saying that those `tⱼ` are part of a regular system of parameters of
`B_𝔭`.

All forms live in the exterior algebra `E` of `Ω_{L/k}`, `L = B[1/∏ⱼ tⱼ]`. Cohomology classes
are recorded through representatives: the theorem gives a function `C` on logarithmic forms
whose values are closed logarithmic forms, and every identity is required modulo the exact
logarithmic forms `d Ω^{i-1}_{B/k}(log S)`. Bijectivity of the induced map
`Ω^i_{B/k}(log S) → H^i` is stated as injectivity and surjectivity modulo exact forms.

The proof works over the image `⊥ : Subalgebra k B` of `k`, because
`MMP.DeRham.exists_logInverseCartier_of_forall_isMaximal` takes its base ring inside `B`. The
conclusion is invariant under an identification of differentials compatible with `d`
(`cartierStatement_of_linearEquiv`), and `Ω[L⁄k] ≃ₗ[L] Ω[L⁄⊥]` is one. Locally at a maximal
ideal the étale coordinates over `k` are transported to coordinates over `⊥` along `k ≃ₐ[k] ⊥`.

*The decomposition: Frobenius twist.* The source states the decomposition on the Frobenius twist
`V^{(1)}`, for the relative Frobenius `V → V^{(1)}`. Because `k` is perfect, the projection
`V^{(1)} → V` is an isomorphism of schemes; it carries `S^{(1)}` to `S` and
`Ω^i_{V^{(1)}/k}(log S^{(1)})` to `Ω^i_{V/k}(log S)`, and composed with the relative Frobenius it
is the absolute Frobenius `F` of `V`. So the statement is made in the derived category of
`𝒪_V`-modules, with `F_* = Scheme.Modules.pushforward (absoluteFrobenius V p hV)`, where
`a ∈ 𝒪_V` acts by `aᵖ`.

*Simple normal crossings.* The components are given by ideal sheaves `Jⱼ` on `V` and `Iⱼ` on `𝒱`.
The divisor is simple normal crossing when, for every finite set `T` of components, the
intersection `⋂_{j ∈ T}` (the subscheme of `⨆_{j ∈ T}`) is smooth of relative dimension
`n - #T`, and empty when `#T > n`; the case `T = ∅` is the smoothness of the ambient scheme.
The lift is a pullback square exhibiting `V` as the closed fibre of `𝒱 → Spec W₂(k)` along
`π : W₂(k) → k`, the zeroth Witt coordinate, with each `Sⱼ` the preimage of `𝒮ⱼ`. The map `π`
is a parameter pinned by `hπ`, since a ring homomorphism cannot be written inside a statement.

*The logarithmic de Rham complex.* Its terms enter as `𝒪_V`-modules `K q` with injective,
`𝒪_V`-linear maps `e`, natural in the open `W`, from `Γ(K q, W)` to the `q`-forms on `W ∩ U`,
`U = V ∖ S`. Their image is cut out by Deligne's criterion: a form `ω` on `W ∩ U` is
logarithmic exactly when `fω` and `f dω` extend over every affine `W' ⊆ W`, for every product
`f = ∏ⱼ cⱼ` of sections `cⱼ` of the ideals `Jⱼ` over `W'`. This determines `K q` up to unique
isomorphism as the subsheaf `Ω^q_{V/k}(log S)` of `j_*Ω^q_{U/k}`. The differential `d` of
`F_*K^•` is a morphism of `𝒪_V`-modules determined by its compatibility with the de Rham
differential, the arrows of `Scheme.Hom.deRhamComplex`.

*Section modules.* The sections of `𝓡(L)` and `𝓜(F, L)` over an open `U ⊆ S` are the section
ring `Stacks.GradedSections.sectionRing` and the graded module
`Stacks.TwistedSections.twistModule` of the restrictions of `L` and `F` to the open subscheme
`f⁻¹(U)`, with the module structure `Stacks.TwistedSections.instModule` given by multiplication
of sections. Both direct images are quasi-coherent, so local finiteness of `𝓜(F, L)` over `𝓡(L)`
is finiteness of these modules over every affine open `U`; this is the form stated. The
invertibility of the restriction of `L` to `f⁻¹(U)`, which the module structure on the twisted
sections requires, is an instance argument; it always holds, the restriction of an invertible
module to an open subscheme being invertible ([Stacks, Tag 0B8L]). Relative semiampleness is
stated as in `MMP.fg_sectionRing_restrict_of_isProjective`: every point of `f⁻¹(U)` lies in the
nonvanishing locus of some section of `L^{⊗ d}` over `f⁻¹(U)`.

## References

* [P. Deligne, L. Illusie, *Relèvements modulo p² et décomposition du complexe de de Rham*,
  Invent. Math. 89 (1987)][DeligneIllusie1987], Théorème 2.1, §4.
* [P. Deligne, *Théorie de Hodge II*, Publ. Math. IHÉS 40 (1971)][Deligne1971], 3.1.
* [H. Esnault, E. Viehweg, *Lectures on vanishing theorems*][EsnaultViehweg1992], §9, §10.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CV), for the section ring.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5L), for the module of
  twisted sections.
-/

@[expose] public section

open KaehlerDifferential TensorProduct

namespace MMP.DeRham

/-- The conclusion of `exists_logInverseCartier`, for a base ring `A` of any universe and any
`B`-algebra `L`. -/
private def CartierStatement (p : ℕ) (A : Type*) {B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    (L : Type*) [CommRing L] [Algebra A L] [Algebra B L] {ι : Type*} (t : ι → B) : Prop :=
  let E := ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A])
  let dlog : ι → Ω[L⁄A] := fun j ↦
    Ring.inverse (algebraMap B L (t j)) • D A L (algebraMap B L (t j))
  let G : Set (Ω[L⁄A]) := Set.range (fun b : B ↦ D A L (algebraMap B L b)) ∪ Set.range dlog
  let logForms : ℕ → Submodule B E := fun i ↦
    Submodule.span B {ω | ∃ v : Fin i → Ω[L⁄A], (∀ m, v m ∈ G) ∧ ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti L i v = ω}
  let closedLog : ℕ → Set E := fun i ↦
    {ω | ω ∈ logForms i ∧
      ∃ x : ⋀[L]^i (Ω[L⁄A]), (x : E) = ω ∧ deRhamDifferential (A := A) i x = 0}
  let exactLog : ℕ → Set E := fun i ↦
    {ω | ω = 0 ∨ ∃ (j : ℕ) (x : ⋀[L]^j (Ω[L⁄A])), j + 1 = i ∧ (x : E) ∈ logForms j ∧
      ((deRhamDifferential (A := A) j x : ⋀[L]^(j + 1) (Ω[L⁄A])) : E) = ω}
  ∃ C : ℕ → E → E,
    (∀ i, ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, C i ω ∈ closedLog i) ∧
    (∀ i, ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, ∀ η ∈ logForms i, C i (ω + η) - (C i ω + C i η) ∈ exactLog i) ∧
    (∀ i (b : B), ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, C i (b • ω) - b ^ p • C i ω ∈ exactLog i) ∧
    (∀ i j, ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, ∀ η ∈ logForms j,
      C (i + j) (ω * η) - C i ω * C j η ∈ exactLog (i + j)) ∧
    C 0 1 = 1 ∧
    (∀ b : B, C 1 (ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (D A L (algebraMap B L b))) -
      ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (algebraMap B L b ^ (p - 1) • D A L (algebraMap B L b)) ∈
        exactLog 1) ∧
    (∀ j : ι, C 1 (ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (dlog j)) - ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (dlog j) ∈ exactLog 1) ∧
    (∀ i, ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, C i ω ∈ exactLog i → ω = 0) ∧
    (∀ i, ∀ z ∈ closedLog i, ∃ ω ∈ logForms i, z - C i ω ∈ exactLog i)

/-! ### Changing the base ring along a surjection

For a surjection `A₁ → A₂` the Kähler differentials `Ω[L⁄A₁]` and `Ω[L⁄A₂]` are identified, and
so are the logarithmic de Rham complexes. -/

section Transport

variable {A₁ A₂ B L : Type*} [CommRing A₁] [CommRing A₂] [CommRing B] [CommRing L]
  [Algebra A₁ L] [Algebra A₂ L] [Algebra B L]

/-- The logarithmic generators over the base `A`. -/
private noncomputable def gens (A : Type*) [CommRing A] [Algebra A L] {ι : Type*} (t : ι → B) :
    Set (Ω[L⁄A]) :=
  Set.range (fun b : B ↦ D A L (algebraMap B L b)) ∪
    Set.range (fun j ↦ Ring.inverse (algebraMap B L (t j)) • D A L (algebraMap B L (t j)))

/-- The logarithmic forms over the base `A`. -/
private noncomputable def logSpan (A : Type*) [CommRing A] [Algebra A L] {ι : Type*} (t : ι → B)
    (i : ℕ) : Submodule B (ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A])) :=
  Submodule.span B {ω | ∃ v : Fin i → Ω[L⁄A], (∀ m, v m ∈ gens (B := B) A t) ∧
    ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti L i v = ω}

variable (ψ : Ω[L⁄A₁] →ₗ[L] Ω[L⁄A₂]) (hψ : ∀ a, ψ (D A₁ L a) = D A₂ L a)

include hψ

private theorem map_mem_gens {ι : Type*} {t : ι → B} {w : Ω[L⁄A₁]} (hw : w ∈ gens A₁ t) :
    ψ w ∈ gens A₂ t := by
  rcases hw with ⟨b, rfl⟩ | ⟨j, rfl⟩
  · exact Or.inl ⟨b, (hψ _).symm⟩
  · exact Or.inr ⟨j, by rw [map_smul, hψ]⟩

private theorem map_ι_smul_D (r c : L) :
    ExteriorAlgebra.map ψ (ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (r • D A₁ L c)) =
      ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (r • D A₂ L c) := by
  rw [ExteriorAlgebra.map_apply_ι, map_smul, hψ]

private theorem map_mem_logSpan {ι : Type*} {t : ι → B} {i : ℕ}
    {ω : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₁])} (hω : ω ∈ logSpan A₁ t i) :
    ExteriorAlgebra.map ψ ω ∈ logSpan A₂ t i := by
  induction hω using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨v, hv, rfl⟩ := hx
    rw [ExteriorAlgebra.map_apply_ιMulti]
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, fun m ↦ map_mem_gens ψ hψ (hv m), rfl⟩
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hx hy
  | smul b x _ hx =>
    rw [AlgHom.map_smul_of_tower]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ b hx

private theorem map_deRhamDifferential {i : ℕ} (x : ⋀[L]^i (Ω[L⁄A₁])) :
    exteriorPower.map (i + 1) ψ (deRhamDifferential (A := A₁) i x) =
      deRhamDifferential (A := A₂) i (exteriorPower.map i ψ x) := by
  have hx : x ∈ Submodule.span ℤ (Set.range fun c : Fin (i + 1) → L ↦
      c 0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti L i fun k ↦ D A₁ L (c k.succ)) := by
    rw [Crystalline.span_range_smul_ιMulti_eq_top (D A₁ L) (span_range_derivation A₁ L) i]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hx
    rw [deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D, exteriorPower.map_apply_ιMulti, map_smul,
      exteriorPower.map_apply_ιMulti]
    have h := deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D (A := A₂) (B := L) i c
    simp only [Function.comp_def, hψ]
    exact h.symm
  | zero => simp only [map_zero]
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => simp only [map_add, hx, hy]
  | smul a x _ hx => simp only [map_zsmul, hx]

private theorem map_mem_closed {ι : Type*} {t : ι → B} {i : ℕ}
    {ω : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₁])}
    (hω : ω ∈ logSpan A₁ t i ∧ ∃ x : ⋀[L]^i (Ω[L⁄A₁]),
      (x : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₁])) = ω ∧ deRhamDifferential (A := A₁) i x = 0) :
    ExteriorAlgebra.map ψ ω ∈ logSpan A₂ t i ∧ ∃ x : ⋀[L]^i (Ω[L⁄A₂]),
      (x : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₂])) = ExteriorAlgebra.map ψ ω ∧
        deRhamDifferential (A := A₂) i x = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨hl, x, rfl, hx⟩ := hω
  exact ⟨map_mem_logSpan ψ hψ hl, exteriorPower.map i ψ x, exteriorPower.coe_map ψ x, by
    rw [← map_deRhamDifferential ψ hψ, hx, map_zero]⟩

private theorem map_mem_exact {ι : Type*} {t : ι → B} {i : ℕ}
    {ω : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₁])}
    (hω : ω = 0 ∨ ∃ (j : ℕ) (x : ⋀[L]^j (Ω[L⁄A₁])), j + 1 = i ∧
      (x : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₁])) ∈ logSpan A₁ t j ∧
      ((deRhamDifferential (A := A₁) j x : ⋀[L]^(j + 1) (Ω[L⁄A₁])) :
        ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₁])) = ω) :
    ExteriorAlgebra.map ψ ω = 0 ∨ ∃ (j : ℕ) (x : ⋀[L]^j (Ω[L⁄A₂])), j + 1 = i ∧
      (x : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₂])) ∈ logSpan A₂ t j ∧
      ((deRhamDifferential (A := A₂) j x : ⋀[L]^(j + 1) (Ω[L⁄A₂])) :
        ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A₂])) = ExteriorAlgebra.map ψ ω := by
  rcases hω with rfl | ⟨j, x, hj, hx, rfl⟩
  · exact Or.inl (map_zero _)
  · refine Or.inr ⟨j, exteriorPower.map j ψ x, hj, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [exteriorPower.coe_map]; exact map_mem_logSpan ψ hψ hx
    · rw [← map_deRhamDifferential ψ hψ, exteriorPower.coe_map]

end Transport

section TransportStatement

variable {A₁ A₂ B L : Type*} [CommRing A₁] [CommRing A₂] [CommRing B] [CommRing L]
  [Algebra A₁ L] [Algebra A₂ L] [Algebra B L]

/-- **The statement does not depend on the base**, along an isomorphism of differentials
compatible with `d`. -/
private theorem cartierStatement_of_linearEquiv (p : ℕ) (φ : Ω[L⁄A₁] ≃ₗ[L] Ω[L⁄A₂])
    (hφ : ∀ a, φ (D A₁ L a) = D A₂ L a) {ι : Type*} (t : ι → B)
    (h : CartierStatement p A₂ L t) : CartierStatement p A₁ L t := by
  have hφs : ∀ a, φ.symm (D A₂ L a) = D A₁ L a := fun a ↦ by
    rw [LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq, hφ]
  set e₁ := ExteriorAlgebra.map (φ : Ω[L⁄A₁] →ₗ[L] Ω[L⁄A₂])
  set e₂ := ExteriorAlgebra.map (φ.symm : Ω[L⁄A₂] →ₗ[L] Ω[L⁄A₁])
  have h₂₁ : ∀ ω, e₂ (e₁ ω) = ω := ExteriorAlgebra.leftInverse_map_iff.2 φ.symm_apply_apply
  have h₁₂ : ∀ ω, e₁ (e₂ ω) = ω := ExteriorAlgebra.leftInverse_map_iff.2 φ.apply_symm_apply
  have ml := fun {i : ℕ} {ω} (hω : ω ∈ logSpan A₁ t i) ↦ map_mem_logSpan _ hφ hω
  have ml' := fun {i : ℕ} {ω} (hω : ω ∈ logSpan A₂ t i) ↦ map_mem_logSpan _ hφs hω
  have mc' := fun {i : ℕ} {ω} hω ↦ map_mem_closed (t := t) (i := i) (ω := ω) _ hφs hω
  have mc := fun {i : ℕ} {ω} hω ↦ map_mem_closed (t := t) (i := i) (ω := ω) _ hφ hω
  have me' := fun {i : ℕ} {ω} hω ↦ map_mem_exact (t := t) (i := i) (ω := ω) _ hφs hω
  have me := fun {i : ℕ} {ω} hω ↦ map_mem_exact (t := t) (i := i) (ω := ω) _ hφ hω
  obtain ⟨C, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8, h9⟩ := h
  refine ⟨fun i ω ↦ e₂ (C i (e₁ ω)), fun i ω hω ↦ mc' (h1 i _ (ml hω)),
    fun i ω hω η hη ↦ ?_, fun i b ω hω ↦ ?_, fun i j ω hω η hη ↦ ?_, ?_, fun b ↦ ?_,
    fun j ↦ ?_, fun i ω hω hC ↦ ?_, fun i z hz ↦ ?_⟩
  · have := me' (h2 i _ (ml hω) _ (ml hη))
    rwa [map_sub, map_add, ← map_add] at this
  · have := me' (h3 i b _ (ml hω))
    rwa [map_sub, AlgHom.map_smul_of_tower, ← AlgHom.map_smul_of_tower] at this
  · have := me' (h4 i j _ (ml hω) _ (ml hη))
    rwa [map_sub, map_mul, ← map_mul] at this
  · change e₂ (C 0 (e₁ 1)) = 1
    rw [map_one, h5, map_one]
  · have e := map_ι_smul_D _ hφ 1 (algebraMap B L b)
    rw [one_smul, one_smul] at e
    change e₂ (C 1 (e₁ _)) - _ ∈ _
    rw [e, ← map_ι_smul_D _ hφs, ← map_sub]
    exact me' (h6 b)
  · change e₂ (C 1 (e₁ _)) - _ ∈ _
    rw [map_ι_smul_D _ hφ, ← map_ι_smul_D _ hφs, ← map_sub]
    exact me' (h7 j)
  · have := me hC
    rw [h₁₂] at this
    rw [← h₂₁ ω, h8 i _ (ml hω) this, map_zero]
  · obtain ⟨ω', hω', hex⟩ := h9 i _ (mc hz)
    refine ⟨e₂ ω', ml' hω', ?_⟩
    have := me' hex
    rwa [map_sub, h₂₁, ← h₁₂ ω'] at this

end TransportStatement

/-! ### The trivial case -/

private theorem cartierStatement_of_subsingleton (p : ℕ) {A B L : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [CommRing L] [Algebra A L] [Algebra B L] [Subsingleton L] {ι : Type*} (t : ι → B) :
    CartierStatement p A L t := by
  have : Subsingleton (ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A])) := Module.subsingleton L _
  have hx : ∀ i (ω : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A])), ∃ x : ⋀[L]^i (Ω[L⁄A]),
      (x : ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄A])) = ω ∧ deRhamDifferential (A := A) i x = 0 := fun i ω ↦
    haveI : Subsingleton (⋀[L]^i (Ω[L⁄A])) := Module.subsingleton L _
    haveI : Subsingleton (⋀[L]^(i + 1) (Ω[L⁄A])) := Module.subsingleton L _
    ⟨0, Subsingleton.elim _ _, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩
  refine ⟨fun _ _ ↦ 0, fun i ω _ ↦ ⟨zero_mem _, hx i 0⟩, fun _ _ _ _ _ ↦ Or.inl
    (Subsingleton.elim _ _), fun _ _ _ _ ↦ Or.inl (Subsingleton.elim _ _),
    fun _ _ _ _ _ _ ↦ Or.inl (Subsingleton.elim _ _), Subsingleton.elim _ _,
    fun _ ↦ Or.inl (Subsingleton.elim _ _), fun _ ↦ Or.inl (Subsingleton.elim _ _),
    fun _ _ _ _ ↦ Subsingleton.elim _ _,
    fun i _ _ ↦ ⟨0, zero_mem _, Or.inl (Subsingleton.elim _ _)⟩⟩

/-! ### The base field inside `B` -/

section Image

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {k : Type*} [Field k] [CharP k p] [PerfectRing k p]
  {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra k B] [Nontrivial B]

private theorem perfectRing_bot : PerfectRing (⊥ : Subalgebra k B) p := by
  have : CharP (⊥ : Subalgebra k B) p := charP_of_injective_algebraMap' k p
  set e := Algebra.botEquivOfInjective (algebraMap k B).injective (R := k) (A := B)
  have : IsReduced (⊥ : Subalgebra k B) :=
    isReduced_of_injective e.toRingHom e.injective
  refine PerfectRing.ofSurjective _ p fun y ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := surjective_frobenius k p (e y)
  refine ⟨e.symm z, e.injective ?_⟩
  rw [frobenius_def, map_pow, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply, ← hz, frobenius_def]

/-- The differentials over `k` and over its image in `B` agree. -/
private noncomputable def kaehlerEquivBot (L : Type*) [CommRing L] [Algebra B L] [Algebra k L]
    [IsScalarTower k B L] : Ω[L⁄k] ≃ₗ[L] Ω[L⁄(⊥ : Subalgebra k B)] :=
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective (KaehlerDifferential.map k (⊥ : Subalgebra k B) L L) ⟨by
    have : Subsingleton (Ω[(⊥ : Subalgebra k B)⁄k]) :=
      KaehlerDifferential.subsingleton_of_surjective k _ fun y ↦ by
        obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Algebra.mem_bot.1 y.2
        exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext ha⟩
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot, ← KaehlerDifferential.range_mapBaseChange, LinearMap.range_eq_bot]
    exact Subsingleton.elim _ _,
    KaehlerDifferential.map_surjective k _ L⟩

end Image

/-- **The logarithmic inverse Cartier isomorphism.** Let `k` be a perfect field of characteristic
`p`, `B` a smooth `k`-algebra and `t : ι → B` a finite family whose zero loci form a reduced
simple normal crossing divisor `S`: at every prime `𝔭`, the differentials of the `tⱼ ∈ 𝔭` are
linearly independent in `κ(𝔭) ⊗_B Ω_{B/k}`. Let `L = B[1/∏ⱼ tⱼ]`. The logarithmic `i`-forms are
the `B`-span in `ExteriorAlgebra L Ω_{L/k}` of the products of `i` one-forms, each either `db`
or `dlog tⱼ`.

Then there is a map `C` that sends each logarithmic `i`-form to a closed logarithmic `i`-form. Its
classes modulo the exact logarithmic forms are additive, Frobenius-semilinear and multiplicative,
with `C 0 1 = 1`, `C(db) ≡ b^{p-1} db` and `C(dlog tⱼ) ≡ dlog tⱼ`. The induced map from
logarithmic `i`-forms to `H^i(F_*Ω^•_{B/k}(log S))` is bijective. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_lc_bpf_log_cartier"]
public theorem exists_logInverseCartier (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {k : Type*} [Field k] [CharP k p]
    [PerfectRing k p] {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra k B] [Algebra.Smooth k B]
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (t : ι → B)
    (hS : ∀ 𝔭 : PrimeSpectrum B,
      LinearIndependent 𝔭.asIdeal.ResidueField
        (fun j : {j : ι // t j ∈ 𝔭.asIdeal} ↦
          ((1 : 𝔭.asIdeal.ResidueField) ⊗ₜ[B] D k B (t j) :
            𝔭.asIdeal.ResidueField ⊗[B] Ω[B⁄k]))) :
    let L := Localization.Away (∏ j, t j)
    let E := ExteriorAlgebra L (Ω[L⁄k])
    let dlog : ι → Ω[L⁄k] := fun j ↦
      Ring.inverse (algebraMap B L (t j)) • D k L (algebraMap B L (t j))
    let G : Set (Ω[L⁄k]) := Set.range (fun b : B ↦ D k L (algebraMap B L b)) ∪ Set.range dlog
    let logForms : ℕ → Submodule B E := fun i ↦
      Submodule.span B {ω | ∃ v : Fin i → Ω[L⁄k], (∀ m, v m ∈ G) ∧ ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti L i v = ω}
    let closedLog : ℕ → Set E := fun i ↦
      {ω | ω ∈ logForms i ∧
        ∃ x : ⋀[L]^i (Ω[L⁄k]), (x : E) = ω ∧ deRhamDifferential (A := k) i x = 0}
    let exactLog : ℕ → Set E := fun i ↦
      {ω | ω = 0 ∨ ∃ (j : ℕ) (x : ⋀[L]^j (Ω[L⁄k])), j + 1 = i ∧ (x : E) ∈ logForms j ∧
        ((deRhamDifferential (A := k) j x : ⋀[L]^(j + 1) (Ω[L⁄k])) : E) = ω}
    ∃ C : ℕ → E → E,
      (∀ i, ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, C i ω ∈ closedLog i) ∧
      (∀ i, ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, ∀ η ∈ logForms i, C i (ω + η) - (C i ω + C i η) ∈ exactLog i) ∧
      (∀ i (b : B), ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, C i (b • ω) - b ^ p • C i ω ∈ exactLog i) ∧
      (∀ i j, ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, ∀ η ∈ logForms j,
        C (i + j) (ω * η) - C i ω * C j η ∈ exactLog (i + j)) ∧
      C 0 1 = 1 ∧
      (∀ b : B, C 1 (ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (D k L (algebraMap B L b))) -
        ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (algebraMap B L b ^ (p - 1) • D k L (algebraMap B L b)) ∈
          exactLog 1) ∧
      (∀ j : ι, C 1 (ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (dlog j)) - ExteriorAlgebra.ι L (dlog j) ∈ exactLog 1) ∧
      (∀ i, ∀ ω ∈ logForms i, C i ω ∈ exactLog i → ω = 0) ∧
      (∀ i, ∀ z ∈ closedLog i, ∃ ω ∈ logForms i, z - C i ω ∈ exactLog i) := by
  intro L E dlog G logForms closedLog exactLog
  change CartierStatement p k L t
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial L with _ | _
  · exact cartierStatement_of_subsingleton p t
  have : Nontrivial B := (algebraMap B L).domain_nontrivial
  have : CharP (⊥ : Subalgebra k B) p := charP_of_injective_algebraMap' k p
  have := perfectRing_bot p (k := k) (B := B)
  have : CharP L p := (CharP.charP_iff_prime_eq_zero (Fact.out : p.Prime)).2 (by
    rw [← map_natCast (algebraMap k L), CharP.cast_eq_zero, map_zero])
  set k' := (⊥ : Subalgebra k B)
  have hu : ∀ j, IsUnit (algebraMap B L (t j)) := fun j ↦
    isUnit_of_dvd_unit (map_dvd _ (Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ j)))
      (IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit _)
  have hglob := exists_logInverseCartier_of_forall_isMaximal p (A := k') (L := L)
    hu ?_
  · exact cartierStatement_of_linearEquiv p (kaehlerEquivBot L)
      (fun a ↦ KaehlerDifferential.map_D k k' L L a) t hglob
  intro 𝔪 h𝔪
  obtain ⟨f₀, hf₀, n, s, ε, hs, het⟩ :=
    exists_etale_mvPolynomial_fin t hS ⟨𝔪, h𝔪.isPrime⟩
  refine exists_isLocalLogCartier_of_etale p (L := L) t 𝔪 hf₀ s ε hs ?_
  set eK := Algebra.botEquivOfInjective (algebraMap k B).injective (R := k) (A := B)
  have hK : ∀ c : k', algebraMap k B (eK c) = c := fun c ↦ by
    have h := eK.symm.commutes (eK c)
    rw [Algebra.algebraMap_self, RingHom.id_apply, eK.symm_apply_apply] at h
    exact (congrArg Subtype.val h).symm
  set e := MvPolynomial.mapEquiv (Fin n) eK.toRingEquiv
  set g := (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := k) fun i : Fin n ↦
      algebraMap B (Localization.Away f₀) (s i)).toRingHom
  have het' : (g.comp e.toRingHom).Etale := by
    simp only [RingHom.etale_iff_formallyUnramified_and_smooth] at het ⊢
    obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := (RingHom.etale_iff_formallyUnramified_and_smooth _).1
      (RingHom.Etale.of_bijective e.bijective)
    exact ⟨h1.comp het.1, h2.comp het.2⟩
  convert het' using 1
  refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun c ↦ ?_) (fun i ↦ ?_)
  · simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe,
      e, MvPolynomial.mapEquiv_apply, MvPolynomial.map_C, g,
      AlgHom.toRingHom_eq_coe, RingHom.coe_coe, MvPolynomial.aeval_C]
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k B (Localization.Away f₀), AlgEquiv.coe_ringEquiv, hK]
    rfl
  · simp [g, e]

/-! ### The Deligne–Illusie decomposition -/

section Decomposition

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry Stacks.Frobenius

universe u

/-- **Deligne–Illusie decomposition for a lifted simple normal crossing pair.** Let `k` be a
perfect field of characteristic `p`, let `f : V ⟶ Spec k` be smooth and proper of relative
dimension `n < p`, and let the ideal sheaves `Jⱼ` define a simple normal crossing divisor
`S = ∑ⱼ Sⱼ`. Suppose `(V, S)` is the closed fibre of a smooth scheme `𝒱` over `W₂(k)` carrying
a relative simple normal crossing divisor `∑ⱼ 𝒮ⱼ` with `Sⱼ = 𝒮ⱼ ∩ V`. Let `K q`, with the
embeddings `e`, be the sheaf `Ω^q_{V/k}(log S)` of logarithmic `q`-forms, and let `d` be the
logarithmic de Rham differential on the Frobenius pushforwards `F_* K q`, where `F` is the
absolute Frobenius of `V`. Then, in the derived category of `𝒪_V`-modules,
`⨁_{q ≤ n} Ω^q_{V/k}(log S)[-q] ≅ F_*Ω^•_{V/k}(log S)`. -/
public theorem nonempty_logDeRham_decomposition_of_wittTwoLift (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]
    {k : Type u} [Field k] [CharP k p] [PerfectField k]
    (n : ℕ) (hpn : n < p)
    {V : Scheme.{u}} (f : V ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProper f] [SmoothOfRelativeDimension n f]
    (hV : IsInCharacteristic V p)
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (J : ι → V.IdealSheafData)
    (hJ : ∀ T : Finset ι,
      SmoothOfRelativeDimension (n - T.card) ((⨆ j ∈ T, J j).subschemeι ≫ f) ∧
      (n < T.card → IsEmpty (⨆ j ∈ T, J j).subscheme))
    {𝒱 : Scheme.{u}} (g : 𝒱 ⟶ Spec (.of (TruncatedWittVector p 2 k)))
    (I : ι → 𝒱.IdealSheafData)
    (π : TruncatedWittVector p 2 k →+* k) (hπ : ∀ x, π x = x.coeff 0) (i : V ⟶ 𝒱)
    (hi : IsPullback i f g (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom π)))
    (hIJ : ∀ j, ∃ φ, IsPullback φ (J j).subschemeι (I j).subschemeι i)
    (hI : ∀ T : Finset ι,
      SmoothOfRelativeDimension (n - T.card) ((⨆ j ∈ T, I j).subschemeι ≫ g) ∧
      (n < T.card → IsEmpty (⨆ j ∈ T, I j).subscheme))
    [HasDerivedCategory.{u} V.Modules]
    (U : V.Opens) (hU : U = ((⨅ j, J j).support).compl)
    (K : ℕ → V.Modules)
    (e : ∀ (q : ℕ) (W : V.Opens), Γ(K q, W) →+ Γ(f.relativeDifferentialForms (q : ℤ), W ⊓ U))
    (he_inj : ∀ (q : ℕ) W, Function.Injective (e q W))
    (he_smul : ∀ (q : ℕ) W (a : Γ(V, W)) (s : Γ(K q, W)),
      e q W (a • s) = V.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W ⊓ U ≤ W)).op a • e q W s)
    (he_res : ∀ (q : ℕ) (W₁ W₂ : V.Opens) (h : W₁ ≤ W₂) (s : Γ(K q, W₂)),
      e q W₁ ((K q).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op s) =
        (f.relativeDifferentialForms (q : ℤ)).presheaf.map
          (homOfLE (inf_le_inf_right _ h)).op (e q W₂ s))
    (he_range : ∀ (q : ℕ) (W : V.Opens) (ω : Γ(f.relativeDifferentialForms (q : ℤ), W ⊓ U)),
      ω ∈ Set.range (e q W) ↔
        ∀ (W' : V.affineOpens) (hW' : (W' : V.Opens) ≤ W) (c : ι → Γ(V, W')),
          (∀ j, c j ∈ (J j).ideal W') →
          (∃ η : Γ(f.relativeDifferentialForms (q : ℤ), W'),
            (f.relativeDifferentialForms (q : ℤ)).presheaf.map
                (homOfLE (inf_le_left : (W' : V.Opens) ⊓ U ≤ W')).op η =
              V.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : (W' : V.Opens) ⊓ U ≤ W')).op (∏ j, c j) •
                (f.relativeDifferentialForms (q : ℤ)).presheaf.map
                  (homOfLE (inf_le_inf_right U hW')).op ω) ∧
          (∃ η : Γ(f.relativeDifferentialForms ((q + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ), W'),
            (f.relativeDifferentialForms ((q + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)).presheaf.map
                (homOfLE (inf_le_left : (W' : V.Opens) ⊓ U ≤ W')).op η =
              V.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : (W' : V.Opens) ⊓ U ≤ W')).op (∏ j, c j) •
                (f.relativeDifferentialForms ((q + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)).presheaf.map
                  (homOfLE (inf_le_inf_right U hW')).op
                    (((f.deRhamComplex).d q (q + 1)).val.app (op (W ⊓ U)) ω)))
    (d : ∀ q : ℕ, (Scheme.Modules.pushforward (absoluteFrobenius V p hV)).obj (K q) ⟶
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward (absoluteFrobenius V p hV)).obj (K (q + 1)))
    (hd : ∀ q : ℕ, d q ≫ d (q + 1) = 0)
    (he_d : ∀ (q : ℕ) (W : V.Opens) (s : Γ(K q, absoluteFrobenius V p hV ⁻¹ᵁ W)),
      e (q + 1) (absoluteFrobenius V p hV ⁻¹ᵁ W) ((d q).app W s) =
        ((f.deRhamComplex).d q (q + 1)).val.app (op (absoluteFrobenius V p hV ⁻¹ᵁ W ⊓ U))
          (e q _ s)) :
    Nonempty ((⨁ fun q : Fin (n + 1) ↦
        (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor V.Modules (q : ℤ)).obj (K q)) ≅
      DerivedCategory.Q.obj ((CochainComplex.of
        (fun q ↦ (Scheme.Modules.pushforward (absoluteFrobenius V p hV)).obj (K q)) d hd).extend
          ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat)) :=
  FrobeniusSplittingData.nonempty_iso_directSum_singleFunctor
    ⟨hpn, hV, J, hJ, 𝒱, g, I, π, hπ, i, hi, hIJ, hI, U, hU, K, e, he_inj, he_smul, he_res,
      he_range, d, hd, he_d⟩

end Decomposition

end MMP.DeRham

/-! ### Finiteness of the section module over a relatively semiample section ring -/

namespace MMP

section SectionModule

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.GradedSections Stacks.TensorPowers Stacks.TwistedSections

universe u

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemePreadditive
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeTensorRightAdditive

attribute [local implicit_reducible] Stacks.TensorPowers.natTensorPow

/-- **Finiteness of the section module over a relatively semiample section ring.**
For a projective `f : Y ⟶ S` over a locally Noetherian `S`, an invertible `L` some positive
power of which is generated by relative sections locally over `S`, and a coherent `F`, the
module `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(f⁻¹(U), F ⊗ L^{⊗ n})` is finite over the section ring
`⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(f⁻¹(U), L^{⊗ n})` for every affine open `U ⊆ S`. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_foundation_relative_semiample_section_module"]
public theorem moduleFinite_twistModule_restrict_of_isProjective {Y S : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ S)
    (hf : IsProjective f) [IsLocallyNoetherian S] (L : Y.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule Y L]
    (hL : ∀ s : S, ∃ U : S.Opens, s ∈ U ∧ ∃ d : ℕ, 0 < d ∧ ∀ y ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ U,
      ∃ t : Γ(natTensorPow L d, f ⁻¹ᵁ U),
        y ∈ Stacks.NonvanishingLocusRestrict.nonvanishingLocusOn (natTensorPow L d) (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) t)
    (F : Y.Modules) [F.IsCoherent] (U : S.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).toScheme (L.restrict (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι)] :
    Module.Finite (sectionRing (L.restrict (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι))
      (twistModule (F.restrict (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι) (L.restrict (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι)) := by
  have : IsProper f := hf.isProper
  obtain ⟨D, hD, N, σ, hσ⟩ := SemiampleSections.exists_generatesStalks_restrict f L hL U hU
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(S, U) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨U, hU⟩
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian Y := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  have : (F.restrict (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι).IsCoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.isCoherent_restrict_of_isOpenImmersion
      (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι F ‹_›
  exact SemiampleSections.moduleFinite_twistModule_of_generatesStalks
    ((f ∣_ U) ≫ hU.isoSpec.hom) _ hD σ hσ _

end SectionModule

end MMP

